# skil hashes file content in several places that must be
# platform-independent: package/SBOM builds, attestation/evidence
# payloads, and test fixtures with pinned checksums.txt digests. Without
# this file, a checkout on Windows (where git's core.autocrlf commonly
# defaults to true) silently rewrites LF line endings to CRLF, changing
# those files' bytes and therefore their digests — this is exactly what
# broke tests/fixtures/*/checksums.txt on a real Windows CI run.
#
# Normalize line endings to LF for text files on checkout, on every
# platform, regardless of the local core.autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Keep archive-like fixtures untouched either way.
*.tgz binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.zip binary
